  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="model 5.3, 5.1, 3.1 I-P5">Every route in ProcedureEndpoints.cs carries 099's step-0 flag on its group (reads included): flagged-external, no systemuser row or a flag-read fault → refused before any read.</constraint>
    <constraint source="model 3.1 I-P5, D-76">Publish, date changes, version retire and Procedure retire: caller Write on the Procedure (Record path, as the caller) AND the billing-admin privilege (BillingAdminAuthorization, CallerHoldsPrivilegeAsync, fail closed). Create: the caller's Create privilege on sprk_procedure (live name casing read and pinned by a test). Reads: caller Read on the Procedure. Writes then run as the BFF application user (I-P2 field security).</constraint>
    <constraint source="model 3.1 I-P1">Dates are DateOnly, half-open [from, to). Publishing version n from D sets the previous Active version's to = D in the same BFF operation; a failure of the second write undoes the first. Overlap with another Active version → 409 procedure.version_overlap, nothing written. Version numbers are assigned by the BFF; a duplicate on the (Procedure, version number) alternate key retries once, then 409.</constraint>
    <constraint source="model 3.1 I-P3, I-P4">Type Rate card without Firm → 400 procedure.firm_required. Once any version is Active, a change to Applies to or Firm → 409 procedure.scope_locked ("Create a new Procedure to change who it governs."), nothing written.</constraint>
    <constraint source="model 3.2, 7.2">Publish needs a Draft version with one Servable Stored File (purpose Procedure source) and an effective-from; otherwise 400 with the field. Publish marks the version's policy versions sprk_publishstate Published and moves sprk_currentversion to the latest published one (display only, ontology-r1 D-14 amendment). RuleSetService edit, publish, IsDraft and Predecessor are keyed per (policy, Procedure Version).</constraint>
    <constraint source="model 7.2 (v2 copies v1)">Copy-forward creates version n+1 as Draft and copies version n's rules as Draft policy versions of the SAME policies under the new version. A rule version n+1 drops stays enabled with no policy version under n+1. Rate-card copy is 085's.</constraint>
    <constraint source="model 3.1 I-P5 (version retire), 8.2">Retiring one version sets it Retired (never selected again); its policies stay enabled; nothing is re-checked; no Signal is closed.</constraint>
    <constraint source="model 15 answer 2 (preview = sweep)">The preview's Signal set comes from the SAME method the close uses: extract SignalClosureService's selection (ReadOpenSignalsAsync's query and predicate) into one internal method that ClosePolicyRetiredNowAsync, ClosePoliciesNotInForceAsync and the preview all call. No second query anywhere (an ArchTest or a test that the preview calls that method). The preview writes nothing.</constraint>
    <constraint source="model 15 answer 2 (counted as the caller)">From that set, map each Signal to its invoice, keep open invoices, and count only those the caller can Read, in one batched GetCallerRightsForRecordsAsync call per page. Response: the warning "Retiring this Procedure will close all related rules and remove pending decisions on active invoices." plus "N open invoices you can see are affected." No "others hidden" number or flag. A rights read that faults → the warning with no count, never the app-only number.</constraint>
    <constraint source="model 3.1 I-P5, 12 D-170">Retire (on confirm): Procedure Retired; each policy of its rule set sprk_enabled = No; then close each policy's open Signals PolicyRetired through the shared method. The action acts on every affected invoice. The result reports the actual closed count, counted as the preview counts (caller-readable open invoices among those whose Signals closed; no count on a rights fault). A close that fails leaves the policy Off, so the job's D-170 sweep closes the rest; the result says the close is incomplete. No re-check, no banner write.</constraint>
    <constraint source="model 7.2 (O-24)">PolicyVersionValidator refuses sprk_procedureversion on an Ontology-domain policy. Billing never writes sprk_policy.sprk_matter.</constraint>
    <constraint source="model 13 (080 row), O-23">sprk_procedure and sprk_procedureversion join RecordCreatorPerson.StampedChildTables and the creator-person script ($SolutionHomes: secure and verify only; 080 created the column), asserting zero non-null values before securing; creator person = the caller. Owner of both: the caller's business-unit team through IRecordOwnershipResolver with no parents (5.1); census lists the writer.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Not in this task: assignments and overrides (089); the resolver (082); drafting re-keyed to the version's Stored File (BillingRuleDraftJobHandler, 075 row of model 12); retiring the Procedure Library upload of POST /rulesets (092, 084). A rule set without sprk_procedure applies to nothing under 082.</constraint>
    <constraint source=".claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md, ADR-010">Placement BFF (B1 caller identity); concrete service registered in AddFinanceModule; publish-size delta; no package; no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
    <constraint source="uac-r2 2026-10-21 (round 113 item 3; task 191)">Procedures are internal-only. Flagged-external systemusers on dev hold the same roles as internal users (Spaarke Basic User, Spaarke Console User, Spaarke Office Add In User) through their business unit's default team. So until uac-r2 task 191 lands, this task adds NO role privilege on sprk_procedure, sprk_procedureversion or sprk_procedureassignment without uac-r2's agreement; all access goes through the BFF.</constraint>
  </constraints>

