  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Read notes/080 and 088 for live names and values; confirm 099's flag type.</step>
    <step order="1">Extract the Signal selection in SignalClosureService; tests that both close paths still close the same Signals.</step>
    <step order="2">ProcedureService: create (with its rule set), version create, copy-forward, publish, date change, version retire, I-P3 / I-P4 checks; RuleSetService re-key.</step>
    <step order="3">Preview and Procedure retire.</step>
    <step order="4">ProcedureEndpoints with authorization; ledger GovernedFile entry; validator refusal; creator-person entries; census.</step>
    <step order="5">Tests (criteria); seeding proof on the preview's caller filter (make it count every invoice; the hidden-invoice test must fail).</step>
    <step order="6">dotnet build and test; Pester pin; publish-size delta; /conflict-check; ontology-r1 and uac-r2 reviews recorded.</step>
    <step order="7">Update TASK-INDEX.md: this task's status cell to "✅ [done]".</step>
    <step order="8">Record deviations in projects/ebilling-r1/notes/081-procedure-version-service.md.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>Model 3.1 I-P5 says "the response never counts or lists invoices" while 15 answer 2 says "the result reports the actual count". This task reports only a caller-scoped count. If a reviewer asks for an app-only count of Signals or invoices, STOP and raise 🔔 Human Input Required.</trigger>
    <trigger>If ontology-r1 refuses the extraction of the selection method in SignalClosureService, STOP; do not write a second query in the BFF.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the Procedure's owner cannot be resolved with no parents through IRecordOwnershipResolver (a census or resolver change needed), STOP and ask uac-r2.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>RuleSetService (Services/Finance/RuleSetService.cs:320) holds rule sets with name, scope, firm, dates and source document; model 3.3 answers the overlap for sprk_procedure and sprk_procedureversion. No service writes either table (new in 080).</existing>
    <extension>RuleSetService is extended for the re-key and the rule set's Procedure; a Procedure service is new because a Procedure is the document and its versions, not the rules (model 3.3, O-1, O-15). The selection method is extracted, not duplicated.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>No Procedure or version can be created or published, so no billing rule is ever in force under the resolver (082), and retiring a Procedure has no safe path (no preview, no reconcile).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">build, test</tool>
    <tool name="pwsh">Invoke-Pester for the creator-person script pin</tool>
    <tool name="conflict-check">before the PR</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">ProcedureService.cs, ProcedureEndpoints.cs, RuleSetService.cs, SignalClosureService.cs, PolicyVersionValidator.cs, RecordCreatorPerson.cs, Set-ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchema.ps1</output>
    <output type="test">ProcedureServiceTests.cs, ProcedureEndpointsTests.cs, RuleSetServiceTests.cs, closure and validator tests, Pester pin, ledger, census</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/ebilling-r1/notes/081-procedure-version-service.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Every ProcedureEndpoints route refuses a flagged-external caller, a caller with no systemuser row and a flag-read fault, before any read (negative); internal callers pass to the next check.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish, date change, version retire and Procedure retire return 403 without the billing-admin privilege, 403 without Write on the Procedure, 403 when the privilege probe faults; with both they succeed. Create returns 403 without the Create privilege.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">I-P1: publishing v2 from D sets v1's to = D; an overlapping date range returns 409 procedure.version_overlap and writes nothing; if the predecessor write fails, the new version is not left Active.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">I-P3 and I-P4: a Rate card Procedure without Firm is refused 400; changing Applies to or Firm after a version is Active is refused 409 procedure.scope_locked; before that it succeeds.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish without a Servable Procedure-source Stored File is refused 400; a valid publish marks the version's policy versions Published and moves sprk_currentversion; a Draft policy version under another Procedure Version is untouched.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Copy-forward: v2 holds Draft copies of every v1 rule under the same policies; a rule removed from v2 before publish stays enabled with no v2 policy version.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Version retire sets Retired, closes no Signal and leaves the policies enabled.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Preview: it calls the shared selection method (test or ArchTest); with 3 affected open invoices of which the caller can Read 2, it returns "2 open invoices you can see are affected" and no other number or hidden flag; a rights fault returns the warning with no count; it writes nothing.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Retire: the Procedure is Retired, every policy of its set is Off, and the open Signals the shared method selects at confirm time are closed PolicyRetired, including those on invoices the caller cannot Read; the result's count is caller-scoped; a Signal that changed since the preview is handled as the close does today.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">PolicyVersionValidator refuses sprk_procedureversion on an Ontology-domain policy and accepts it on a Billing policy.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Creator-person agreement test and Pester pin pass with sprk_procedure and sprk_procedureversion; census passes with the new writer; ledger lists ProcedureEndpoints.cs with each route's basis.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Seeding proof recorded for the preview's caller filter; publish-size delta recorded; no package; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named above. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Two adversarial-review passes (auth, security). 089 reuses the shared selection method and the preview counting for override removal; copy the counting into one internal helper here so 089 calls it. The old 081 (rule-set scope, BU writes, secure family for every set) is superseded by EB-D-148; its secure-child work for record-scoped sets is 089's. ontology-r1 080 review 2026-10-21: sprk_procedureversion.sprk_procedure is an alternate-key column and cannot be field-secured, so this task pins (test over the role privileges) that no non-BFF role holds Create or Write on sprk_procedureversion or sprk_procedureassignment. 080 hand-off 2026-10-21: 080 creates sprk_createdbyperson on sprk_policy and sprk_policyversion but does not publish sprk_policy; Set-ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchema.ps1 (this task) lists and publishes sprk_policy and sprk_policyversion. 080's verify fails by design if any role a flagged-external user holds gains a privilege on the three Procedure tables (uac-r2 rule above). ontology-r1 080 re-check 2026-10-21 (K2): before securing sprk_policy.sprk_createdbyperson (and sprk_policyversion's), assert zero non-null values (the D-173 condition); the column stays unpublished and unsecured until this task. K1 (080): Assert-ScopeOptionsIntact fails only on missing sprk_scope options, not extras; the final verify catches extras.</notes>

